  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-26T04:00:06.996Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have 36 objects in my world which each sync a few strings. The strings aren't huge; less than 150 characters apiece. Whenever a peer joins, or after a sync occurs when a peer is already on, the master starts spewing an insane amount of log spam and the peers stop receiving syncs for those objects. This is a SEVERE show-stopper for my world. Syncing this data is absolutely vital for my world's operation and I cannot currently continue working on it without this being fixed.\nA sample of the log spam; it's the same thing repeated constantly: https://gist.github.com/briman0094/b452a1a054ed7ee4d49dc3fb6adc6646",
